# The Red Paperclip trade graph.
#
# This file is the world. Hubs and their prose live in script.yaml; every
# item, every trader, and every trade you can make lives here, in three
# kinds of line:
#
#   <item>: <name>                    an item you can hold
#   <trader>: <name> @ <hub>          a trader, standing in one hub
#   <held> -> <trader> -> <offered>   a trade
#
# A trader has exactly one thing to give, so the offered item is declared
# once and every later line naming that trader inherits it:
#
#   red_paperclip -> mira -> fish_pen   Mira gives the pen for the paperclip
#   brass_doorknob -> mira              ...and for a doorknob too
#
# A trade line may carry the line the journal prints, d2-style, after a
# colon. Attributes hang off a dotted key: `.here` is what you see when a
# trader is in front of you, `.gone` is what you see once they have traded
# their one thing away, and `.ending` is how the story ends if you are still
# holding that item when nobody will trade for it any more. `.gone` is
# optional; without it a trader says plainly that they have nothing left.
#
# Paste it into d2 or read it top to bottom. Both work.


# ── items ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

red_paperclip: a red paperclip
fish_pen: a fish-shaped pen
brass_doorknob: a hand-turned brass doorknob
crab_trap: a folding crab trap
accordion: a wheezing accordion
bicycle: a green three-speed bicycle
camp_stove: a two-burner camp stove
neon_sign: a neon OPEN sign
pa_system: a portable PA system
espresso_machine: a temperamental espresso machine
kayak: a fibreglass sea kayak
outboard_motor: a 9.9 horsepower outboard
panel_van: a rust-free panel van
freight_pallet: a pallet of unclaimed freight
glider: a wooden-winged glider
auckland_tickets: two open-jaw tickets to Auckland

# ── the ends of the line ────────────────────────────────────────────────

lighthouse_keys: the keys to the Rock Point light
lighthouse_keys.ending: |
  Nobody trades for a lighthouse. You climb the stair on the first
  evening and find the lamp housing swept, the log book open, and one
  ruled line left for you at the bottom of the page.

film_role: a speaking part in a feature
film_role.ending: |
  Nobody trades for a speaking part; it is yours or it is nothing. Two
  years later a stranger on a ferry will place your face and be unable
  to say from where.

ostrich_share: a one-third share in an ostrich farm outside Otorohanga
ostrich_share.ending: |
  Nobody at this end of the world will trade you anything for a third
  of an ostrich farm in the Waikato, which is how you come to be
  standing in one at six in the morning, being looked at.

sourdough_starter: a jar of hundred-year-old sourdough starter
sourdough_starter.ending: |
  Nobody trades for a starter. You feed it flour and water on the
  Sunday and it comes up like it never left, and that is the end of the
  travelling.

stuffed_marlin: a mounted blue marlin
stuffed_marlin.ending: |
  Nobody wants the marlin. Not one person. It goes over the door where
  the coats should be and stays there for the rest of your life.


# ── the harbour ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

mira: Mira, who mends nets @ harbor
mira.here: Mira has a net across her knees and a spool of orange twine.
mira.gone: Mira has the paperclip worked into the net and nothing else to spare.

finn: Finn at the boat racks @ harbor
finn.here: Finn is re-lashing a rack that does not need re-lashing.

gunnar: Gunnar, the harbourmaster @ harbor
gunnar.here: The harbourmaster watches the channel from the office step.

red_paperclip -> mira -> fish_pen: Mira works the paperclip into a torn net, hands you the pen, and does not look up again.
brass_doorknob -> mira: Mira turns the doorknob over twice, keeps it, and gives you the pen.

bicycle -> finn -> kayak: Finn wheels the bicycle away and points you at the kayak on the bottom rack.
accordion -> finn: Finn takes the accordion for the clubhouse and lets the kayak go.

outboard_motor -> gunnar -> lighthouse_keys: The harbourmaster needs a motor more than he needs a lighthouse he is not allowed to sell. The keys are cold.
panel_van -> gunnar: The harbourmaster has wanted a van since the spring. He signs the light over to you on the office step.


# ── the market ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

wick: Wick, at the tarp table @ market
wick.here: Wick is arranging brass on a tarp in no order at all.
wick.gone: Wick has nothing brass left on the tarp worth trading for.

cass: Cass, in off the day boat @ market
cass.here: Cass has crates to shift and is short of hands.

pia: Pia, who bakes @ market
pia.here: Pia is out of things to sell by nine and stays until noon anyway.
pia.gone: Pia gave away the jar and will not start another this year.

hollis: Hollis, closing the cafe @ market
hollis.here: Hollis is boxing up a cafe one shelf at a time.

red_paperclip -> wick -> brass_doorknob: Wick clips the paperclip to a ledger he will never read again and lets you take the doorknob.
fish_pen -> wick: Wick has a granddaughter who would like the fish pen. The doorknob is yours.

fish_pen -> cass -> crab_trap: Cass signs for a delivery with the fish pen and gives you the trap out of the stern.
accordion -> cass: Cass wants the accordion for the boat. Take the trap.

brass_doorknob -> pia -> sourdough_starter: Pia has been shutting that door with a screwdriver for a year. She gives you the jar and tells you how to feed it.
camp_stove -> pia: The stove is worth more than the jar and Pia says so twice before trading anyway.

neon_sign -> hollis -> espresso_machine: Hollis takes the sign for the new place and lets the machine go. It works when it wants to.
pa_system -> hollis: Hollis is done with the cafe but not with the band. The machine is yours.


# ── the ring road garage ────────────────────────────────────────────────

teo: Teo, who fixes everything @ garage
teo.here: Teo is fixing something that is not his and not urgent.

dot: Dot in the parts bay @ garage
dot.here: Dot knows what is in every drawer and will not tell you.

olsen: Olsen in the engine bay @ garage
olsen.here: Olsen has an outboard clamped to a barrel of water, running.

rusev: Rusev, under the van @ garage
rusev.here: Rusev is under a van that no longer needs him under it.

brass_doorknob -> teo -> camp_stove: Teo has a door that has been shut with a nail since March. The stove is in the back.
crab_trap -> teo: Teo takes the trap for his brother and hands over the stove.

camp_stove -> dot -> neon_sign: Dot trades the sign off the old shop front for a stove she can use at the counter.
bicycle -> dot: Dot wants the bicycle for the parts run. The sign comes down.

crab_trap -> olsen -> outboard_motor: Olsen is owed a trap by someone who left. Yours settles it, and the outboard is running when you get it.
kayak -> olsen: Olsen takes the kayak for the lake house and clamps the outboard to your side of the bench.

outboard_motor -> rusev -> panel_van: Rusev wants the outboard for a boat he has not bought. The van starts on the second turn.
espresso_machine -> rusev: Rusev's waiting room has been coffee-less since the machine before this one. Take the van.


# ── miller college ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

junie: Junie, who plays for change on the quad @ campus
junie.here: Junie has an open case and eleven dollars in it.

gus: Gus at the bike rack @ campus
gus.here: Gus has three bicycles and needs none of them.

devi: Devi, of the film society @ campus
devi.here: Devi is arguing about a shooting schedule with nobody in particular.

petra: Petra, who is making a feature @ campus
petra.here: Petra is making a feature and is four days behind.

fish_pen -> junie -> accordion: Junie signs a form with the fish pen and gives you the accordion, which she says is beyond her.
camp_stove -> junie: Junie plays outdoors in October. The stove is worth more to her than the accordion.

fish_pen -> gus -> bicycle: Gus needs a pen for the sign-out sheet more than he needs a third bicycle.
crab_trap -> gus: Gus takes the trap for a house he is moving into and wheels the green three-speed out.

accordion -> devi -> pa_system: Devi has wanted an accordion for the soundtrack since August. The PA is under the stage.
neon_sign -> devi: The sign is going in the film. The PA is yours.

panel_van -> petra -> film_role: Petra needs a van for four days. She offers you a van's worth of speaking part, and writes it down so it is real.


# ── the rail halt ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

yusuf: Yusuf on the freight dock @ station
yusuf.here: Yusuf is signing for things that were never ordered.

marta: Marta in the ticket office @ station
marta.here: Marta has the only working clock on the platform.

lost_property: the lost-property window @ station
lost_property.here: The lost-property window is open, which is rare.

panel_van -> yusuf -> freight_pallet: Yusuf trades the pallet nobody has claimed for a van the depot has needed all year. He does not tell you what is on it.
bicycle -> yusuf: Yusuf trades the unclaimed pallet for something he can ride to the far end of the yard.

espresso_machine -> marta -> auckland_tickets: The tickets have been unclaimed for six weeks and the ticket office has been coffee-less for longer.
glider -> marta: Marta's brother flies. The tickets are yours, open-jaw, dated whenever you like.

freight_pallet -> lost_property -> stuffed_marlin: The window takes the pallet without comment and gives you the largest thing behind it.
kayak -> lost_property: The window will not take the kayak as lost property but will take it as a trade. You get the marlin.


# ── the grass airfield ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

bree: Bree, who flies the mail @ airfield
bree.here: Bree has the mail plane open and half of it on the grass.

ilse: Ilse, who charters @ airfield
ilse.here: Ilse charters to the islands and back, weather allowing.

whina: Whina, going home to Otorohanga @ airfield
whina.here: Whina is going home for good and is one seat short of it.

freight_pallet -> bree -> glider: Bree takes the pallet on the strength of the manifest alone and rolls the glider out of the far shed.
kayak -> bree: Bree has wanted a kayak longer than she has wanted the glider gone.

glider -> ilse -> auckland_tickets: Ilse has a hangar and no glider in it. The tickets are open-jaw and she has held them since March.
panel_van -> ilse: Ilse needs a van at the strip more than she needs two seats she cannot use.

auckland_tickets -> whina -> ostrich_share: Whina needs the second seat. What she has to trade is a third of a farm at the other end of the world, and she is entirely serious about it.
